WEBVTT

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:14.914
Hi, friends. Gani here. This is Snake Breath.

00:00:14.914 --> 00:00:21.827
Sit tall in your chair. Feet flat on the floor.

00:00:21.827 --> 00:00:25.975
Hands resting on your desk. Shoulders soft.

00:00:25.975 --> 00:00:30.123
Take one slow breath with me… and let it go.

00:00:30.123 --> 00:00:39.802
This is a breathing practice with a snake shape. You breathe in through your nose. Then you let the air out in a long, soft hiss — ssss — like a snake sliding slowly through the grass.

00:00:39.802 --> 00:00:50.864
The hiss is just air. Soft and slow, like a leak, never a push. It lasts as long as the air lasts — and when the air is gone, the hiss is done. Nobody stretches it or squeezes out more.

00:00:50.864 --> 00:01:03.308
The hiss floats out into your own space, toward nobody. And it can be quiet — a nearly silent hiss is a whole, complete practice.

00:01:03.308 --> 00:01:08.839
Nothing is ever held. The air moves in, the air moves out. That is the whole shape. Here we go.

00:01:08.839 --> 00:01:21.284
Round one. Breathe in through your nose… and hiss it out, soft and long: ssss.

00:01:21.284 --> 00:01:33.728
Round two. In… and out on your snake breath: ssss. Slow, like sliding through grass.

00:01:33.728 --> 00:01:46.172
Round three. In… and hiss: ssss. Let your shoulders drop as the hiss slips away.

00:01:46.172 --> 00:01:57.234
Round four. In through your nose… and out: ssss, until the air runs out on its own.

00:01:57.234 --> 00:01:58.617
One last round, on your own. In… and hiss as long as the air lasts. Then let the hiss go, and just breathe the way your body wants to.

00:01:58.617 --> 00:02:11.061
Now hear the rules that keep this practice yours. The hiss is a gentle guide — it is never a test.

00:02:11.061 --> 00:02:23.505
If your hiss is shorter, or quieter, your practice is still complete. Your breath, your pace. And this is never a contest — not the longest, not the quietest, not the slowest, not the biggest.

00:02:23.505 --> 00:02:33.184
And if anything ever feels dizzy, or tight, or strange, the move is simple: breathe normally. Normal breathing is always allowed, at any second. It is never a failure.

00:02:33.184 --> 00:02:34.567
Notice how your breathing feels now, all on its own. Nothing to fix. Nothing to hold.

00:02:34.567 --> 00:02:44.246
In through your nose. Out on a long, soft hiss. Then let it be.

00:02:44.246 --> 00:02:51.160
Shoulders soft. Let your body rest.

00:02:51.160 --> 00:02:56.690
Hands down. One more slow breath… and let it go.

00:02:56.690 --> 00:03:03.604
Eyes open. Look around your classroom.

00:03:03.604 --> 00:03:10.518
You're ready for what's next.
